<title>USA: Royce Labs doesn't see suit hurting results.</title>
<headline>Royce Labs doesn't see suit hurting results.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royce Laboratories Inc said it did not expect the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission's lawsuit against three of its employees to have a material adverse impact on the company.</p>
<p>The SEC said on Friday it charged three Royce employees and three others with alleged insider trading in the fall of 1991 and spring of 1992 related to the generic drug Piroxicam.</p>
<p>Royce said in a statement released over the weekend that it was surprised by the civil suit because it had been led to believe by the three employees that they were seeking to resolve the matters amicably.</p>
<p>Royce said it had not yet seen a copy of the complaint.</p>
<p>&quot;The filing of this suit is not expected to have a material adverse impact on the company, its business, financial position or results of operations,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
